-- setting's Comments string into `${flyway:defaultSchema}.`, which Flyway would resolve to
-- `__mj_BizAppsCommon.Company` on every host. It is restored to the text metadata/ declares.
--
-- -- ENTITY PERMISSIONS: THE ONE HAND EDIT, AND A FIX FOR V202609020500 ----------------------
--
-- metadata/entities/.activity-sync-run-details.json keys its two EntityPermission records by
-- `@lookup:` (EntityID + RoleID), because CodeGen creates permission rows with newsequentialid()
-- IDs that differ on every database. The generator resolves that lookup on the generation database
-- and bakes ITS row ID into `SET @ID = '...'`, so on any other database the spUpdateEntityPermission
-- matches no row and silently does nothing. V202609020500 shipped exactly that for the UI row
-- ('2C47433E-F36B-1410-84AF-00D21EB65DCC'); the Integration row reached metadata/ later. On a
-- clean install of this chain without this seed, UI has CanRead and Integration has full CRUD on
-- Activity Sync Run Details, where metadata/ declares UI none and Integration CanCreate only.
-- Found by diffing a clean-room install of this chain against the generation database.
--
-- Both calls here therefore resolve @ID on the host from (EntityID, RoleID), and THROW rather than
-- no-op if there is not exactly one such row. Entity and Role IDs are stable across databases
-- (declared by migrations), so the lookup is the same one metadata/ states.
-- =============================================================================================

